  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="38f8291a-8f6b-5cab-812f-a2a81f94bcd6" activityNameId="8c7d29fa-0f8b-57fd-ae73-ac7eee63aeab" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Crude coconut oil, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Crude coconut oil, at plant
data based on the ECOSOL study of the European surfactant industry. Allocations in multioutput processes were made, using the relative mass outputs of products.;
UUID: bfcc9b7d-6cbc-3596-a544-9691fe09e112
This module contains material and energy input, production of waste and emissions for the steps from the harvested coconuts to the crude coconut oil (i.e. the coconut halving, extraction of water, meat removal &amp; shell production, drying and the oil extraction). Water consumption and infrastructure have been estimated.
Location: Data based on coconut oil mills in Phillippines
Technology: Average technology, typical for Phillippines conditions in the mid 90s
Time period: data of published literature
Production volume: worldwide 2'900 kt in 1993
Sampling: &lt;null&gt;
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: &lt;null&gt;
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_bfcc9b7d-6cbc-3596-a544-9691fe09e112.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
